    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">An algebraic fraction is a fraction where the numerator and/or denominator contains algebraic expressions like letters (variables) and numbers. Examples include <em>\\( \\frac{3x}{5} \\)</em> and <em>\\( \\frac{x+2}{x-1} \\)</em>. These fractions combine the idea of fractions with algebraic expressions.</p>",
